  "_readme": "Single authority for model routing (OS-02b-core). Never hand-edit pins, activation or role capabilities \u2014 use `cortextos model switch|pin|unpin|activation|role-capability`, which does a CAS write and journals an event. Agent config.json `model` fields are LEGACY. TWO DIFFERENT CAPABILITY FIELDS LIVE ON A ROLE AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE: `required_capabilities` is matched against a model entry's `capability_tags` during resolution, so a value there that no entry carries makes the role UNRESOLVABLE; `role_capabilities` describes the ROLE itself (what it participates in, e.g. `continuous-improvement` for weekly Kaizen enrollment), is never matched against any model, and therefore can never break resolution. Manage it with `cortextos model role-capability add|remove|list` (no restart \u2014 a capability changes no route).",
